217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Applications: Fans, pumps, compressors, crushers, cutting machines, conveyors and other general-purpose mechanical equipment in petroleum, chemical, coal, power generation, metallurgy, transportation, textiles, pharmaceuticals and food/grain processing industries.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The inner side of the motor frame, around the stator winding ends, is provided with internal cooling fins that effectively improve heat dissipation. The internal airflow is driven by the fan at the non-drive end through rotor ventilation holes. The air flows rapidly over the inner cooling fins of the frame and end shields, providing additional cooling. Heat exchange between the frame and the outside air further improves the cooling effect. Four air channels direct the flow toward the drive end, resulting in more uniform heat dissipation through the internal and external circuits \(see Figures 1 and 2\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
